// # openOODA Website — Anchor for Agents
//
// Logline: Public website for the openOODA polyrepo, served from
//          GitHub Pages at openooda.org.
//
// Setup: Static site. The deploy workflow pushes `main` to GitHub
//        Pages as-is. No build step. The website content is hand-
//        maintained; per-repo pages are pulled from each repo's
//        `docs/` directory and hand-synced into `pulled/{repo}.json`.
//
// Beats:
//   1. index.html — single-page app shell (the SPA renders into
//      <main id="content">).
//   2. 404.html — not found page; same shell as index.html.
//   3. src/main.js — the SPA: router, theme, install copy handler,
//      gen bar, the background fighter-jet dogfight animation.
//   4. styles/main.css — 9 theme palettes, layout, install box,
//      gen-bar, dogfight canvas, sky starfield.
//   5. assets/favicon.svg — browser tab icon.
//   6. assets/open-graph.png — social card image (OpenGraph +
//      Twitter).
//   7. sitemap.xml and robots.txt — crawler metadata.
//   8. llms.txt — public LLM context (single canonical manual).
//   9. pulled/{repo}.json — per-repo docs loaded by the SPA when
//      a sub-menu item is clicked. 7 routes today: openOODA,
//      ooda, std, opm, cli, lsp, mcp. oodac + runtime are
//      "coming soon" placeholders (no JSON yet).
//  10. Sub-menu: 8 polyrepo repos in first-principles order —
//      ooda, std, opm, cli, lsp, mcp; oodac + runtime as
//      "coming soon" pending gemini's extraction from ooda/.
//
// Layout (one concept, one location):
//
//   /
//     index.html, 404.html, sitemap.xml, robots.txt, llms.txt,
//     CNAME, LICENSE, VERSION, ANCHOR.oo
//     assets/   — static images (favicon, social card)
//     pulled/   — 7 JSON files, one per route
//     src/      — the SPA
//     styles/   — the single CSS file
//     .github/  — deploy workflow
//
// Banned names (no mod/util/helpers/common/misc/stubs/lib/interface/
// types/impl): enforced. Every directory has an ANCHOR.oo. Every
// file is under 256 lines. No compat layers, no fallbacks, no
// dead-code stubs — old code is killed, not kept.
